    {
      "id": "xgm2zey",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Election of the President"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zynahgo",
      "content": "• The President is elected indirectly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6w6xtg4",
      "content": "• Members of an Electoral College elect the President."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jky5kvs",
      "content": "• Electoral College consists of elected members of Parliament and elected members of State Legislative Assemblies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gsqwc5n",
      "content": "• The election uses proportional representation by means of single transferable vote."
    },
    {
      "id": "7txu2u8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Qualifications for President"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1crkqn0",
      "content": "• Must be a citizen of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z5fnh7n",
      "content": "• Must be at least 35 years old"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rv0szli",
      "content": "• Must be qualified for election as a member of Lok Sabha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "olj8bnu",
      "content": "• Must not hold any office of profit"
    },
    {
      "id": "fzqel39",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Powers of the President"
    },
    {
      "id": "0642wr4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Executive Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "The executive power of the Union shall be vested in the President and shall be exercised by him either directly or through officers subordinate to him in accordance with this Constitution.",
      "id": "mmj301f"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qocmj5t",
      "content": "• Appoints Prime Minister and Council of Ministers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s0l1dfk",
      "content": "• Appoints Governors, Judges of Supreme Court and High Courts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rrzauko",
      "content": "• Appoints Attorney General and Comptroller and Auditor General"
    },
    {
      "id": "uo8tobo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Legislative Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ixjn5k0",
      "content": "• Summons and prorogues Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gytk2z5",
      "content": "• Addresses Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dlles0y",
      "content": "• Gives assent to bills"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mvn3vwy",
      "content": "• Can promulgate ordinances under Article 123"
    },
    {
      "id": "yqqpaau",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Financial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "President (Article 72)",
        "Governor (Article 161)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Death Sentence",
          "Can pardon, reprieve, or commute death sentences",
          "Cannot pardon death sentence (can only suspend, remit, or commute)"
        ],
        [
          "Court-Martial",
          "Has power to pardon sentences imposed by military courts",
          "Has no power regarding Court-Martial sentences"
        ],
        [
          "Law Jurisdiction",
          "Pertains to offences against Union laws",
          "Pertains to offences against State laws"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "t742jee"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q8e4tyr",
      "content": "• No money bill can be introduced without President's recommendation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cj5p34n",
      "content": "• President causes the Union Budget to be presented in Parliament"
    },
    {
      "id": "56atvkj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Judicial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7p4ur67",
      "content": "• Can grant pardon, reprieve, respite, remission and commutation of punishment under Article 72"
    },
    {
      "id": "miazdvg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Emergency Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3jyr5vf",
      "content": "• National Emergency (Article 352)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "low3h8h",
      "content": "• President's Rule in states (Article 356)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8r6to3j",
      "content": "• Financial Emergency (Article 360)"
    },
    {
      "id": "e7cstal",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Impeachment of the President"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iwurli7",
      "content": "• The President can be removed for violation of the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vpigs7d",
      "content": "• The impeachment process can be initiated in either House of Parliament."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Nominated members of both Houses of Parliament and State Assemblies do NOT participate in the Presidential election, but nominated members of Parliament DO participate in impeachment.",
        "An Ordinance promulgated under Article 123 must be approved by Parliament within 6 weeks from its reassembly.",
        "Only the President can grant pardon in cases of death sentences and sentences by Court-Martial (military courts)."
      ],
      "id": "f0oq53j"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rzooach",
      "content": "• A two-thirds majority is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "5x3gp57",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "724rnag",
      "content": "• First President of India – Dr. Rajendra Prasad"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tzv2fd8",
      "content": "• President is elected indirectly"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lzuiynt",
      "content": "• Term of President – 5 years"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "azqjnz9",
      "content": "• Oath administered by Chief Justice of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uinp5cv",
      "content": "• Article 72 deals with pardoning power"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
